 "_comment": [
  "Per-suite cost model for tools/verif/soc_shards.py, PLAIN (uninstrumented) soc_all_ci run, the",
  "one cocotb.yml shards (bead 9ayu.2).  Same format as soc_shard_weights.json (instrumented).",
  "Source: the 'Run soc_all' step log of cocotb.yml job 117623384863 (run 39109839710, 4-vCPU",
  "ubuntu-latest, warm ccache, 2081 s of make).  A suite's run_s is the wall time between the end",
  "of the previous results block and the end of its own, so a Verilator build it triggered is",
  "included (warm ccache: a few seconds); `group` build_s is a COLD-cache estimate (a PR that",
  "edits rtl/ recompiles the model once per shard) and only steers how builds are shared.",
  "soc_uart_boot (709 s as one module) is split in the three SOC_CI_SPLITS units in the same",
  "proportions as the instrumented measurement (890:710:390), since the per-test split was only",
  "measured instrumented.  Suites absent here cost default_run_s, so a new suite never breaks the",
  "sharding.  Runner speed varies ~2x between runs (soc_uart_boot: 709 s here, 1394 s in run",
  "39113206673); the weights only need to be proportional.  Refresh from a newer job log when the",
  "printed per-shard estimate drifts from the measured shard times.  The fourth slice,",
  "test_load_verify_8n1_back_to_back (shm5, #314), is 317 s x 384.2/448.7: its plain-sim time",
  "measured in #314's cocotb run 39113206673, scaled by test_load_verify_jump_and_run's ratio."
 ],
